sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch12-05> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "In Fusulina the breadths of successive whorls stand in the nearly constant ratio 1 : 1.5, which corresponds to a logarithmic spiral with a constant angle of about 86°, like that of ammonites.";
    dc:type "mathematical-law";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Fusulina whorls increase in ratio 1:1.5, a spiral of constant angle about 86°";
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "Fusulina: b_{n+1}/b_n \\approx 1.5 \\Rightarrow \\alpha \\approx 86^\\circ";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "D’Arcy Wentworth Thompson, On Growth and Form (1st ed., Cambridge: Cambridge University Press, 1917), Chapter XII, “The Spiral Shells of the Foraminifera”; topic “Logarithmic spiral of foraminiferal shells”. Scope: fusulinid Foraminifera (Fusulina cylindrica, F. Böcki)"
}
